[75.450311, "o", "83:def get_tolerance_for_precision(precision: str | torch.dtype) -> float:\r\n85:    Get the tolerance from a string representing the percision.\r\n86:    These tolerances are inspired by torchbench (PyTorch Benchmarking Suite): \r\n96:        # torchbench states for bf16 and fp16, use 1e-3 as tolerance and 1e-2 if it's too strict. \r\n97:        # @todo: Let user configure own tolerance as an option\r\n370:def _process_input_tensor(input, device, backend=\"cuda\", precision=torch.float32):\r\n495:    init_inputs = [_process_input_tensor(x, device, backend, precision) for x in init_inputs]\r\n618:                inputs = [_process_input_tensor(x, device, backend, precision) for x in inputs]\r\n663:        inputs = [_process_input_tensor(x, device, backend, precision) for x in inputs]\r\n767:            inputs = [_process_input_tensor(x, device, backend, precision) for x in inputs]\r\n801:                # now we will return the tolerance from get_tolerance_for_precision\r\n802:                tolerance = get_tolerance_for_precision("]
[75.450366, "o", "precision)\r\n804:                if not torch.allclose(\r\n805:                    output, output_new, atol=tolerance, rtol=tolerance\r\n"]
